---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const description = `Support for ${site.name}. Email ${site.publisher} at ${site.email}.`;
---

<Base title="Support" description={description}>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="kicker">Support</p>
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      {site.name} is available on the <a href={site.appStoreUrl}>App Store</a>. The Android version is
      <a href="/news/play-store-review">in review on Google Play</a>. This is the support page for
      the game.
    </p>

    <h2>Write to us</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. {site.publisher} reads that address.
    </p>
    <p>In your note, include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>What you expected to happen</li>
      <li>What happened instead</li>
      <li>Your device model</li>
      <li>Your operating system version</li>
      <li>The app version, if the game shows it</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A screenshot helps when the question is about a level or a purchase.</p>

    <h2>Progress</h2>
    <p>
      The game does not have an account. Your journey is saved on the device only. We cannot look
      up a save, move it to a new phone, or restore it after the app is deleted. How to erase that
      save is on <a href="/data">Your Data</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases, when the game offers them, are billed by Apple or Google. For a refund, start in
      that store's purchase history. If a purchase unlocked the wrong thing, email us and include
      the store order number if you have it. Do not send a full card number.
    </p>

    <h2>Policies</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>,
      <a href="/advertising">Advertising Policy</a>, and
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> are published with this site.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
